  closest to slope 1: K = 5.0 (exclude |w-w0| < 0.500 rad/s), slope 1.0251, rms 0.0876
  K is O(1)-O(10) in units of the resonance half-width, so the partition
  is the resonance itself: the near-resonant spectrum diffuses (it is
  Dtilde) and the off-resonant spectrum erodes (it is alpha_eff).  Adding
  both over the whole axis double-counts the resonant band.
